  "status": "applied",
  "key": "worker_count",
  "value": "4",
  "rationale": "Eight feeds are queued and all workers share one upstream account. With no load-test or account-limit evidence on record, setting worker_count to 4 is the highest count that is demonstrably sustainable: it halves the backlog per cycle while keeping concurrent upstream requests well below the untested ceiling of 8, reducing the risk of rate-limiting or account suspension on the shared account."
}
